0,Azha language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azha_language,"Azha is spoken by the Phula people, but it is not a Phula language and is a Sani–Azha language, closely related to Sani, Axi and Azhe. Samei of Kunming may be related.",Azha,Sino-Tibetan
1,"Tibetan Music, Healing Music, Relaxation Music, Chakra ...Tibetan Music, Healing Music, Relaxation Music, Chakra ...Azha language — GrokipediaStream AZHA music | Listen to songs, albums, playlists for ...Tibetan Music & Audio — Stream & Download Traditional Music ...(PDF) Sound correspondences of the ’Azha dialect of Thewo ...Azha language - Wikipedia",https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PszSx4HvKAA,"Jul 16, 2017 · Both Tibetan music and Shamanic music use continuous sounds and the flute to create healing music, spa music, stress relief music, study music, peaceful music, relaxing music, and yoga music. Jul 15, 2015 · Tibetan Healing Music, Meditation Music, Relaxing Music for Stress Relief, Background Music, 3266C 432Hz + 528Hz - Fall Into Deep Sleep in 5 Minutes, Whole Body Regeneration, Remove Insomnia The Azha language belongs to the Sino-Tibetan language family, within the Tibeto-Burman branch, and is further classified under the Loloish (also known as Ngwi or Yi) languages. Play AZHA and discover followers on SoundCloud | Stream tracks, albums, playlists on desktop and mobile. Stream rare recordings of traditional Tibetan instruments, monastic chanting, and contemporary Tibetan artists. Abstract This article provides an exhaustive list of systematic sound correspondences between Literary Tibetan (LT) and the ’Azha dialect of Thewo-smad Tibetan. Azha is spoken by the Phula people, but it is not a Phula language and is a Sani–Azha language, closely related to Sani, Axi and Azhe. Samei of Kunming may be related. What is Tibetan meditation music? Tibetan meditation music, as provided by Yellow Brick Cinema, is calming music used for meditation. It functions as ambient music, promoting inner peace for the body-mind. This instrumental music is also known as deep healing music, as it releases positive energy and clears subconscious negativity, making it ideal for yoga practice. What is Tibetan flute music used for? Tibetan flute music is used for healing, yoga, spa, stress relief, mindfulness, sleep, or simply to relax and enjoy. Listening to this music is like undergoing guided meditation, allowing you to relax. Can Tibetan flute music help you fall asleep? Tibetan flute music, which includes flute music and occasionally the sound of Tibetan singing bowls, is powerful sleep music and can help you relax and sleep. This calming music, often referred to as Zen music, can also be used for chakra balancing or to open your chakra to help you achieve mindfulness. Is Azha a Loloish language? Azha is one of the Loloish languages spoken by the Yi people of China . In Azha, the words for ‘goat’, ‘eat’, and ‘drink’ are innovative (Pelkey 2011:377). Luojiayi Azha /mɛ33 xɛ33/ ‘goat’, /la̠45/ ‘eat’, /ŋɨ33/ ‘drink’ are not derived from Proto-Ngwi * (k)-cit L ‘goat’, *dza² ‘eat’, and *m-daŋ¹ ‘drink’.",Azha,Sino-Tibetan
